      {
        "id": "p44-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Differentiate both sides of the binomial expansion above.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4(1+x)^3={}^4C_1+2{}^4C_2x+3{}^4C_3x^2+4{}^4C_4x^3$.",
          "worked": "The binomial coefficients are constants. Differentiating each term gives\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(1+x)^3&=0+{}^4C_1+2{}^4C_2x+3{}^4C_3x^2+4{}^4C_4x^3\\\\&={}^4C_1+2{}^4C_2x+3{}^4C_3x^2+4{}^4C_4x^3.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "By substituting $x=1$, show that ${}^4C_1+2({}^4C_2)+3({}^4C_3)+4({}^4C_4)=4\\times2^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "${}^4C_1+2{}^4C_2+3{}^4C_3+4{}^4C_4=4\\times2^3=32$.",
          "worked": "Substitute $x=1$ into the differentiated identity:\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(1+1)^3&={}^4C_1+2{}^4C_2(1)+3{}^4C_3(1)^2+4{}^4C_4(1)^3\\\\4\\times2^3&={}^4C_1+2{}^4C_2+3{}^4C_3+4{}^4C_4.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe sum of each coefficient multiplied by its exponent index is the row index times half the sum of the whole row.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "By substituting $x=-1$, show that ${}^4C_1-2({}^4C_2)+3({}^4C_3)-4({}^4C_4)=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "${}^4C_1-2{}^4C_2+3{}^4C_3-4{}^4C_4=0$.",
          "worked": "Substitute $x=-1$ into the differentiated identity:\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(1-1)^3&={}^4C_1+2{}^4C_2(-1)+3{}^4C_3(-1)^2+4{}^4C_4(-1)^3\\\\4(0)^3&={}^4C_1-2{}^4C_2+3{}^4C_3-4{}^4C_4\\\\0&={}^4C_1-2{}^4C_2+3{}^4C_3-4{}^4C_4.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe alternating sum of each coefficient multiplied by its exponent index is zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
